md:2059:> Fuel counts completed guest instructions. One `run-fuel` invocation executes at most `n` instructions per visited task, at most one scheduler round per visited inactive task, and at most one bridge step per visited task. A bridge result never restarts execution inside that invocation. No wall-clock bound is claimed for an instruction, host function, stream constructor, variable resolution, bridge step or scheduler sweep. The VM has no clock and converts no time to instructions; `dao.lease` owns liveness and the composition chooses `n`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2101:   A1-A6, T1, K1-K3, E1-E2, X1, P1-P4 one tampered frame built from a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2478:10. **Budgeted children.** Preempt long and nested initializers; lift/lower running children under receiver admission; continue to linked. Count actual instruction transitions and assert at most `n` per visited task and `n × t` overall. No child receives a second budget inside one invocation.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2978:| A1 | §4.1 | the public API as landed: `segment`, `space`, `lift-state`, `lower-state`, `canonical-task`, `kernel-task`, `lower-defect`, `lift-task`, `lower-task` and the rest; `lift-act`/`lift-tail`/`lower-act`/`lower-tail` superseded | engineer deviation 1, accepted by codex: one dispatching entry per direction |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:193:cursor, and may write through the one writer handle. None knows the others\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md:330:**`tail?` is a slot of `:application` only.** The one reader of the tail\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust.md:1232:- A1. Its status header (`targets.md:3-15`) and section 3.7.1 describe\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust.md:1236:- A2. Section 3.2's Rust types are superseded by section 4 here (sparse\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust.md:1238:- A3. T-D2 gains a clause: a kernel-side translation of an admitted\ndocs/design/yin.vm.rust.md:1241:- A4. T1's \"no `unsafe`\" is scoped to the